/-
  BHModesOnset: the exact onset of the negative region of V_S− for D = 6, ℓ = 2 (bh-modes results/onset/, BHM-016/017)
  in Lean (session-L, 2026-10-22). Private under the bh-modes quiet rule. The request is the bh-modes lead's second
  message of 2026-10-22, §3 item (b).
  Sources: results/onset/PREREG.md (sha256 in lean/SOURCES.tsv) §1–2 and RESULT.md; TARGET.md §1 for U₋, δ and x_H.
  Setting: ℓ = 2, m = 6; for μ ∈ [0, 1], w = 7μ/(6 + μ²) = √(1 − q²), δ = (1 − μ²)/(5(6 + μ²)), x_H = 2/(1 + w), x = t x_H.
  A finding on the way: after cancelling common factors, U₋ = F(t, μ)/((μ + 1)³(μ + 6)) with F of degree (4, 4) and
  24 terms (`param_U`), and F(1, μ) = 1024(μ + 15)(10μ³ − 11μ² + 228μ − 45) (`g_factor`). The record's F has degree
  (4, 104) because it keeps factors that cancel. So the positivity needs only three Bernstein boxes of a degree-(4, 4)
  polynomial, with simple endpoints (`box1`–`box3`).
  What is proved (all in ℝ, the irreducibility in ℚ[X]):
  - O5: s = 1 + 2mδ satisfies s² = 1 + 4mq²/25; s > 0 and δ ≥ 0 on [0, 1]; w is continuous and strictly increasing
    from 0 to 1; √(1 − q(μ)²) = w; x_H = 2(6 + μ²)/((μ + 1)(μ + 6)); every q ∈ [0, 1] is some q(μ) (`param_of_q`); and
    TARGET.md's δ is δ(μ) there (`delta_of_q`).
  - O1: p = 10μ³ − 11μ² + 228μ − 45 is strictly increasing, with exactly one real root μ_*, in
    (0.19893240974, 0.19893240975); (6 + μ²)⁶ C(q(μ)²) = p(μ) K(μ) with C = 3025Y³ − 31521Y² + 99792Y − 68796, so
    C(q_*²) = 0; C has exactly one real root; q_* ∈ (0.9730564367, 0.9730564368); both cubics are irreducible over ℚ.
  - O2 (`O2`): for 0 ≤ q with q² ≤ q_*², TARGET.md's δ and 0 ≤ x ≤ x_H(q): U₋(x) ≥ 0. In (t, μ) (`O2_mu`):
    F(t, μ) ≥ 0, with equality only at (t, μ) = (1, μ_*).
  - O3 (`O3`): for q ≤ 1 with q² > q_*²: U₋(x_H(q)) < 0.
  - O4 (`O4`): Kodama–Ishibashi (6.24)'s bracket at the horizon is 4(4μ − 3)/(μ + 1): > 0 for q < 3/5, = 0 at
    q = 3/5, < 0 for q > 3/5.
  The section "Generated" (F, Q, K and the Bernstein forms B1–B3 with their splits) is printed by oracle/gen_onset.py.
  Lean checks every generated identity by `ring`; nothing generated is trusted.
  Not proved here: E0 (it is in BHModesA1.lean and BHModesExtremal.lean), and the statements in the record that use
  Arb or its 45-digit isolating interval. Here the interval is 10⁻¹¹ wide.
-/
